    <h2 class="section-title">What affects the price?</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Timber:</strong> oak, walnut or another hardwood, chosen for each piece.</li>
      <li><strong>Finish and paint:</strong> natural timber, hand-painted, or spray-painted in the workshop. The type of paint makes a real difference to the cost, so it's discussed with you for each project.</li>
      <li><strong>Size and layout:</strong> the number of cabinets, and any larger pieces such as islands, larders, dressers and appliance housings.</li>
      <li><strong>The room:</strong> old houses with uneven walls and floors take more scribing and fitting time.</li>
      <li><strong>Other trades:</strong> whether you would like Joel to coordinate plumbing, electrics, flooring or building work alongside the fitting.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The most reliable way to get a figure is a short conversation followed by a site visit. Send a few photos and rough measurements, and <strong><em>Joel will give you an honest view of whether your plans fit your budget</em></strong>.</p>
  </div>
